WEBVTT

00:01:32.012 --> 00:01:33.032
Oh, I see him move.

00:01:33.964 --> 00:01:34.224
Yeah.

00:01:35.276 --> 00:01:36.216
Eight on the nine.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.300
And then your king comes up and that plays the queen.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:41.880
Will you leave these cards alone?

00:01:43.244 --> 00:01:45.244
You think you can show me something?

00:01:50.284 --> 00:01:52.284
Why don't you ask me what the flowers are for?

00:01:56.044 --> 00:01:56.944
All right, Mr. Bones.

00:01:57.452 --> 00:01:57.652
Bye.

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:58.868
the flowers for.

00:02:00.668 --> 00:02:02.608
Well, this is kind of an anniversary gobble.

00:02:03.612 --> 00:02:05.852
Do you know we've been together just two years today?

00:02:07.804 --> 00:02:08.844
Two years too much.

00:02:10.812 --> 00:02:12.312
Flowers are for dead people.

00:02:21.468 --> 00:02:21.968
He's a loser!

00:02:25.244 --> 00:02:27.384
How often did I tell you not to put a hat on the bed?

00:02:27.804 --> 00:02:28.844
Because it's bad luck.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:35.540
Oh, hats on the bed and spilling the salt and black cats and walking under ladders.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.440
You make your own bad luck.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:43.070
Yeah? Where's the coffee that I passed two hours ago?

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.960
Right there by your side.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.180
It's been there all the time.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:55.260
Oh, it.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.520
Yesterday, it was too hot.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:02:59.940
Never mind what I...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.000
I said yesterday...

00:03:01.596 --> 00:03:04.316
One day it's so hot that you burn your mouth, the next day it's so cold.

00:03:04.476 --> 00:03:05.356
Then you freeze it!

00:03:06.044 --> 00:03:06.884
I'll get some more.

00:03:17.852 --> 00:03:19.852
go to my boy

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:20.560
Adiós.

00:03:22.524 --> 00:03:24.084
I feel fine, thank you.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.300
How do you feel, Gabo?

00:03:26.876 --> 00:03:28.296
Gabo would feel better.

00:03:28.544 --> 00:03:29.904
if he wouldn't have to play.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.180
Patterson this week.

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:35.244
You wouldn't be playing Patterson, dear, if you called Petrit, the agent.

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:37.120
He has better time for you.

00:03:37.324 --> 00:03:37.724
Yeah.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.040
Why should I card him?

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:41.820
Let him call me.

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:44.748
They should be glad to get an act like mine.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.920
They can't get gobbles every day.

00:03:55.212 --> 00:03:56.212
I thought it was too hot.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.600
If I want anything done right, I've got to do it myself.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.790
How are you fixed for steady company?

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.830
Otto, how often did I tell you not to be so fresh?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.230
Okay, Chief.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:18.720
How are you fixed for steady company?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.620
Otto, now that's enough.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:27.640
I'll put you away, ladies and gentlemen.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:33.080
I will now do the impossible.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:40.080
I will smoke a cigarette and drink water

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:44.910
and at the same time use my voice.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.720
Very well done.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:11.950
All right, Professor.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:58.620
My dose bent, and my best gal said, shalom, belts.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.160
This is off.

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:49.450
He told me to pray, did I?

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:17.560
And you were rotten, too, for all you stupid, hungering idiots I've ever seen in my life.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.720
Say, somebody ought to knock that guy's block off.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.240
Yeah, I'd like to do it myself.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:04.840
Curse of mankind!

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:36.820
How often did I tell you how and when to put the props on the stage?

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.360
Are you so stupid that you will never learn?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.430
But I did exactly as you told me.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:45.580
You did not. Don't say you did when you did not.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:47.340
But I did.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.220
You did not. Did I tell you to drop the train?

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.240
No. I won't stand for your talking back to me like this.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.270
Who the devil do you think you are anyway?

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.160
Well, I will talk back to you.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.360
I won't stand it any longer.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.390
Oh, you won't, huh?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.340
Well, let me tell you something.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.480
I'm the greatest living artist in my line in the whole world,

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:15.380
and I'm not going to have my act spoiled by you.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:21.530
Your act, your act, always your act.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.300
Oh, you're a fool.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.600
You're so wrapped up in yourself

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:27.160
that you're blind to anyone else.

00:09:27.830 --> 00:09:29.310
It's always you, you, you.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:29.830
Keep quiet.

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.550
I won't have you saying such things to me.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:39.660
It's bad. It's my act.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.060
No, it's bad, they blame me for it,

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.600
and you're the one that makes it bad, will you?

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:47.620
Oh, whenever the act goes wrong,

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.180
I'm the one you always blame for it.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:51.730
Because you're always to blame.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.060
The gabboos are at it again, honey.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:09:59.980
Really? The poor dame.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:07.490
Yeah, he blames her for everything. She seems like a nice dame, too.

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:09.610
Oh, that guy's cuckoo.

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:13.890
Well, he must be. Well, he talks to that dummy like it was another person.

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:16.550
Yeah, can you beat it? Talking to a dummy.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:18.780
Must be something wrong with his stomach.

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:22.470
Stomach nothing. Something wrong with his skull.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:24.910
But that guy's got a screw loose shirt.

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:26.430
It's none of our business.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.660
I won't stand for it any longer.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.550
Oh, you won't?

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.020
No, I won't.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:40.660
And if you weren't such a helpless fool,

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.720
I'd leave you so quick it'd make your head swim.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:44.530
So?

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.030
Well, let me tell you something.

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:50.670
I don't care when you go, where you go,

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:52.550
and the quicker, the better.

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:53.680
You're doing it.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.480
You mean that?

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:02.390
I mean that.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:11.310
Then I guess I'd better go.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:24.680
That's all the appreciation you have for someone who's always tried to do what was right.

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:27.920
Then you don't deserve consideration.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.060
Who asked you for consideration?

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:36.780
I don't want to think of you. You go.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.210
Where could you go? What could you do without me?

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:46.560
I'm the act, not you. Everything depends on me.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.560
Well, I'm not depending on you any longer.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.930
I was getting along all right before I met you.

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:59.980
Then remember this, I can still sing and I can still dance.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.670
Go ahead. Go on. Nobody's stopping you.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.420
I need you to stay that long.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.290
Oh, I only stayed because I...

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.090
Oh, I don't know why I stayed.

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:21.500
Little Otto there is the only human thing about you.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.210
I don't think it. I know it.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:29.960
Oh, I've tried...

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:34.030
It's so hard to understand you, Garbo, but you're impossible.

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:42.570
The only sweet things you have ever said to me have come from Otto.

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:52.660
I'm quitting the act tonight. I might do better. I know I can't do any worse.

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:59.920
What would you do without me? Go on, get out!

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:01.580
What do I care?

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:04.910
Right, Gabbo.

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:11.750
If that's all the two years we've been together mean to you, I'm sorry.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:19.590
See, that guy's been beefing ever since he opened here.

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:23.580
If you think I'm tough to get along with, you ought to get a load of him.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:24.930
Don't do so bad.

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:56.060
I'm sorry to leave you because you're the only thing about him that seems to have a soul

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:01.680
Even though you are only made of wood.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.990
And if you're as great as you think you are,

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:11.010
why aren't you playing the real theater?

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:13.150
You're doing better things.

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:19.240
You'll mind your own business and go as you said you would.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:22.190
I'll show you.

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:24.610
I'll show them all.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.940
Whether I'm the great Gabo or not.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:29.800
No.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:39.420
But remember this, to get along, to succeed, forget yourself once in a while.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:44.520
Think of someone else. Give in some time.

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:57.780
And listen, we only take out of this life what we put into it.

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:11.570
Bye.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:52.130
You know we can't back him.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:56.750
Mom, don't you know that?

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:24.270
I thought that would coax her to stay.

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:29.560
Looks like she's gone this time for good.

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:37.320
What do I care? Do I need her? No.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:43.060
Do I need anyone? No.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:53.180
He won't be far. She'll be back.

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:59.080
Not this time, Garbo. I don't think so.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.940
You don't think so.

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:02.690
Did I ask you?

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:15.080
Girl, quit the act.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.140
She left him flat.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:19.860
Well, who's that he's talking to now?

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:21.350
Cut me again.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:22.970
He always does that.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:25.540
That guy is sure nuts.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.710
You are not going to let her worry you, are you?

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:36.330
Worry me?

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:42.840
Nothing, Otto. Nothing in this world can worry me.

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:44.120
Says you.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:47.850
Yes, says me. Says me.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:17:59.780
Oh, shut up.

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:03.010
You don't need a drink, Gavo.

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.350
No, I didn't ask you, did I?

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:19.430
You were too, Gavo.

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:22.340
Too hasty with her.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.200
Too hasty?

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:26.520
She spoiled my act.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:28.660
She's a fool.

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:29.980
Oh, no.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:33.680
You are the fool, Garo.

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:35.840
That's enough, Odo.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.070
Do you want me to put you out, too?

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:47.250
Louse, fool.

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.340
Must admit she was sweet.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.040
She helped us, too.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:18:59.920
She comes.

